## 4. What This Unlocks for AdSense

| Signal | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Unique `<title>` per page | ❌ Generic | ✅ Keyword-rich, unique |
| Unique `<meta description>` | ❌ Raw HTML excerpt | ✅ Structured, informative |
| Scripture reference in metadata | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| Keyword signals for contextual ads | ❌ None | ✅ Reformed, Theology, Bible |
| Open Graph title for social | ❌ Raw title | ✅ Full branded title |
| `keywords` meta for Bing/AdSense | ❌ None | ✅ 13 targeted keywords/page |

> [!TIP]
> AdSense uses the page's `<title>`, `<meta description>`, `<meta keywords>`, and the visible `<h1>` to determine **which ads to display**. By including *"Reformed preaching"*, *"Metropolitan Tabernacle"*, *"Prince of Preachers"* etc., we maximize the chance of receiving high-CPM ads from Christian publishers, Bible app companies, seminary courses, and religious book publishers — the most valuable ad category for this niche.

